# PGlite writes a directory per database. Four of them were committed by accident
# in phase 2, when `scripts/migrate.mjs` still had a "run as a script" guard that
# fired inside the bundled CLI and read argv[2] — a command name — as a data
# directory. The guard is fixed; this is belt and braces for anything that lands
# a database at the repo root.
/*.pglite

# THE SETTINGS ENCRYPTION KEY, and anything else the app writes beside it.
#
# `settings-store.ts` mints a 0600 key file under the data directory and every
# secret in `policy_settings` — the OpenRouter key, an Azure key, a bridge
# credential — is AES-GCM encrypted against it. Committing the key would make the
# encrypted column decorative: the repository is public, and a database copy plus
# this file is the same as no encryption at all.
#
# `.data/` above covers the default POLICY_DATA_DIR; this covers the key
# directory, which sits at `data/policy-keys` when nothing overrides it. Caught
# as an untracked file on 2026-09-19, before a `git add -A` swept it in.
/data/

# Throwaway probes at the repo root. They have to live here rather than in a
# temp directory, because `playwright` and `jszip` only resolve from inside the
# project — and one of them was committed in phase 11 before this rule existed.
/.*.mjs

# Staged by `npm run stage:app` for a Databricks App deploy.
/.app/
